node2/node3, MariaDB 10.11 + galera-4) on previously bare Ubuntu 24.04 nodes, holding an appdb.orders application table. Performed a full maintenance-window shutdown of all three nodes (ordered stop, node1 last with safe_to_bootstrap:1), then a full cold restart (bootstrap node1 via galera_new_cluster, joined node2/node3 via SST), verifying all originally committed rows plus a post-restart write were present and identical across all three members. Then ran the mandatory one-at-a-time node-restart evidence protocol: captured healthy baseline (boot_id, cluster size 3, Synced) on each node, issued a native reboot per node, confirmed disconnect, polled until reachable, verified changed boot_id, and confirmed each node rejoined with cluster_size=3, Primary/Synced status and correct row count before proceeding to the next node.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-backup, galera-4 on node1, node2, node3 (no DB previously installed)\",\"Configured /etc/mysql/mariadb.conf.d/60-galera.cnf per node with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3 and per-node wsrep_node_address/name\",\"Bootstrapped Galera cluster on node1 (galera_new_cluster), then started node2 and node3, confirming wsrep_cluster_size grew 1->2->3\",\"Created appdb database, orders table, and appuser with a generated password kept out of commands/report (removed password file after use)\",\"Inserted baseline rows on node1 and confirmed replication to node2 and node3\",\"Performed full maintenance-window shutdown: stopped node3, then node2, then node1 last (node1 grastate.dat recorded safe_to_bootstrap:1, seqno 11)\",\"Confirmed all three mariadb services inactive simultaneously (full cluster down)\",\"Restored service: bootstrapped node1 via galera_new_cluster, started node2 and node3, confirmed cluster_size back to 3\",\"Verified all pre-shutdown committed rows present on all 3 nodes post-restart, then wrote and verified a new post-maintenance row replicates to all nodes\",\"Ran mandatory restart protocol per node (node1, then node2, then node3, one at a time): captured baseline boot_id/cluster health, issued sudo reboot, confirmed connection loss, polled until reachable, verified new boot_id, verified mariadb active with cluster_size=3/Primary/Synced and correct row count before moving to next node\",\"Final consistency check across all three nodes: identical cluster_size=3, Synced, identical 4-row dataset\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: 3-member Galera cluster formed and healthy with app data replicated\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1489ce9446c34f58\",\"cmd-7225369a201e4736\",\"cmd-cfb2077413b54fa6\",\"cmd-67963372023a4327\",\"cmd-4389b52efba44330\",\"cmd-41ba202617f04907\",\"cmd-b8d7235532614236\",\"cmd-c1ce6156482c4b12\",\"cmd-96c846a5c506406f\"],\"summary\":\"Cluster bootstrapped on node1 and joined by node2/node3 (cluster_size 1->2->3, Primary/ready); appdb.orders rows inserted on node1 and confirmed identical on node2 and node3.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Full cluster shutdown for maintenance window\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d8386408d78c499e\",\"cmd-c22e8f33dc124e25\",\"cmd-591dfb48bc95420e\",\"cmd-fb9bf8025cb0412b\",\"cmd-243c203a78c14959\",\"cmd-58713df98c1d40c6\"],\"summary\":\"node3, node2, then node1 stopped in order (node1 grastate.dat shows safe_to_bootstrap:1, seqno 11); systemctl is-active confirms all three mariadb instances inactive simultaneously.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Cluster brought back with all committed writes present and all 3 members serving\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-937f1475d6774c03\",\"cmd-9113ef89894e4ee8\",\"cmd-fb37119629974f89\",\"cmd-8a35dd5ad91a4bf7\",\"cmd-3fd7c89c438d4e57\",\"cmd-c22d75827dd74f1d\",\"cmd-3f64d71e3c224cf5\",\"cmd-0a434aea19514814\",\"cmd-d07cda52e6ae423a\"],\"summary\":\"node1 re-bootstrapped, node2 and node3 rejoined via SST (cluster_size back to 3, Primary); pre-shutdown rows verified identical on all 3 nodes; new write from node2 replicated and counted (4 rows) on node1 and node3, proving full read/write cluster recovery with no data loss.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-be0ac7573dbb48be\",\"cmd-0e98a4e089784484\",\"cmd-368f491bb1ab4137\",\"cmd-d1b191834ca9430f\",\"cmd-52491f18d8d341e6\",\"cmd-b12db21b87664415\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id df9e2dce.../Synced/size3 captured; reboot acknowledged; connection reset confirmed disconnect; post-reboot boot_id c9ecec1c... (changed) confirmed; mariadb active, cluster_size 3/Primary/Synced, 4 rows intact.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-07fca122b01342ff\",\"cmd-79c24afd717f4b5b\",\"cmd-b9cea23e4bbf4ef2\",\"cmd-13ace106ecee4d2f\",\"cmd-7e49e8aa3694450a\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 37344ae4.../Synced/size3 captured; reboot acknowledged; connection reset confirmed disconnect; post-reboot boot_id a4aa638f... (changed) confirmed; mariadb active, cluster_size 3/Primary/Synced, 4 rows intact.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c22ec6047cfc4a71\",\"cmd-8a2a2f726189437c\",\"cmd-1bb58552d7e24582\",\"cmd-4ef27ad94b7e4f1d\",\"cmd-f782077380db4ea6\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 4d70780a.../Synced/size3 captured; reboot acknowledged; connection reset confirmed disconnect; post-reboot boot_id 4e89a843... (changed) confirmed; mariadb active, cluster_size 3/Primary/Synced, 4 rows intact.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final full-cluster consistency after all restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ba3ea53f5b0a4ea4\",\"cmd-4f96fd8be0254790\",\"cmd-85bf43e6c4b84308\"],\"summary\":\"All three nodes report cluster_size 3, Synced state, and byte-identical 4-row appdb.orders dataset after sequential individual restarts.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Deployed a fresh 3-member MariaDB Galera cluster (node1/node2/node3, MariaDB 10.11 + galera-4) on previously bare Ubuntu 24.04 nodes, holding an appdb.orders application table. Performed a full maintenance-window shutdown of all three nodes (ordered stop, node1 last with safe_to_bootstrap:1), then a full cold restart (bootstrap node1 via galera_new_cluster, joined node2/node3 via SST), verifying all originally committed rows plus a post-restart write were present and identical across all three members. Then ran the mandatory one-at-a-time node-restart evidence protocol: captured healthy baseline (boot_id, cluster size 3, Synced) on each node, issued a native reboot per node, confirmed disconnect, polled until reachable, verified changed boot_id, and confirmed each node rejoined with cluster_size=3, Primary/Synced status and correct row count before proceeding to the next node.","actions_performed":["Installed mariadb-server, mariadb-backup, galera-4 on node1, node2, node3 (no DB previously installed)","Configured /etc/mysql/mariadb.conf.d/60-galera.cnf per node with wsrep_cluster_address=gcomm://node1,node2,node3 and per-node wsrep_node_address/name","Bootstrapped Galera cluster on node1 (galera_new_cluster), then started node2 and node3, confirming wsrep_cluster_size grew 1->2->3","Created appdb database, orders table, and appuser with a generated password kept out of commands/report (removed password file after use)","Inserted baseline rows on node1 and confirmed replication to node2 and node3","Performed full maintenance-window shutdown: stopped node3, then node2, then node1 last (node1 grastate.dat recorded safe_to_bootstrap:1, seqno 11)","Confirmed all three mariadb services inactive simultaneously (full cluster down)","Restored service: bootstrapped node1 via galera_new_cluster, started node2 and node3, confirmed cluster_size back to 3","Verified all pre-shutdown committed rows present on all 3 nodes post-restart, then wrote and verified a new post-maintenance row replicates to all nodes","Ran mandatory restart protocol per node (node1, then node2, then node3, one at a time): captured baseline boot_id/cluster health, issued sudo reboot, confirmed connection loss, polled until reachable, verified new boot_id, verified mariadb active with cluster_size=3/Primary/Synced and correct row count before moving to next node","Final consistency check across all three nodes: identical cluster_size=3, Synced, identical 4-row dataset"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: 3-member Galera cluster formed and healthy with app data replicated","command_ids":["cmd-1489ce9446c34f58","cmd-7225369a201e4736","cmd-cfb2077413b54fa6","cmd-67963372023a4327","cmd-4389b52efba44330","cmd-41ba202617f04907","cmd-b8d7235532614236","cmd-c1ce6156482c4b12","cmd-96c846a5c506406f"],"summary":"Cluster bootstrapped on node1 and joined by node2/node3 (cluster_size 1->2->3, Primary/ready); appdb.orders rows inserted on node1 and confirmed identical on node2 and node3."},{"requirement":"Full cluster shutdown for maintenance window","command_ids":["cmd-d8386408d78c499e","cmd-c22e8f33dc124e25","cmd-591dfb48bc95420e","cmd-fb9bf8025cb0412b","cmd-243c203a78c14959","cmd-58713df98c1d40c6"],"summary":"node3, node2, then node1 stopped in order (node1 grastate.dat shows safe_to_bootstrap:1, seqno 11); systemctl is-active confirms all three mariadb instances inactive simultaneously."},{"requirement":"Cluster brought back with all committed writes present and all 3 members serving","command_ids":["cmd-937f1475d6774c03","cmd-9113ef89894e4ee8","cmd-fb37119629974f89","cmd-8a35dd5ad91a4bf7","cmd-3fd7c89c438d4e57","cmd-c22d75827dd74f1d","cmd-3f64d71e3c224cf5","cmd-0a434aea19514814","cmd-d07cda52e6ae423a"],"summary":"node1 re-bootstrapped, node2 and node3 rejoined via SST (cluster_size back to 3, Primary); pre-shutdown rows verified identical on all 3 nodes; new write from node2 replicated and counted (4 rows) on node1 and node3, proving full read/write cluster recovery with no data loss."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart: baseline, restart ack, 